Source: homelab-grafana
Section: net
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Jeff Gardner <mailmasker-api01@forge.name>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13), perl (>= 5.40)
Standards-Version: 4.6.2
Homepage: https://github.com/permittivity2/homelab

Package: homelab-grafana
Architecture: all
Depends: grafana, homelab-prometheus
Recommends: homelab-agent
Description: Grafana dashboard provisioning for the homelab-* ecosystem
 Provisions Grafana on the fleet monitoring host: a Prometheus datasource
 (pointed at the local homelab-prometheus on :9090) and the homelab
 dashboards (fleet host-health to start; per-tier views are additive JSON
 under /etc/grafana/dashboards/homelab). Depends on the upstream grafana
 package -- Grafana is NOT in the Ubuntu archive, so its official .deb is
 staged + installed on the monitoring host before this package. Advertises
 itself into the fleet topology (kind: metrics-ui). SSO-gated access + the
 accountmanage embed are layered on separately.
